From b55dd0f7992990d3292e134d9d6ce4d31a8c657c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gtguerreiro-max <295622337+gtguerreiro-max@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 20:11:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ui: system dialogs answer to the pad and the keyboard

A message box could only be answered with the mouse or the touch screen: on a Steam Deck in
Game Mode the pad did nothing (Asura's Wrath's "saved data does not exist" box), and on a PC
Enter did nothing either. ImGui now navigates with the keyboard and the gamepad: the default
button is selected when the box opens, the D-pad or the left stick moves between buttons, A or
Enter presses one, B or Escape takes the last (escape) button and cancels a keyboard prompt.
The pad is read past the title's input block (IInputSystem::GetStateForUI, added at the end of
the interface so the earlier slots keep their places), and buttons held when a dialog opens are
ignored until released. A message box's text wraps at 32 times the font size (about 45 characters) instead of
one word a line, and its answer is logged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
